<p>I like this idea, it feels very unique and even personal in a way that most SCP articles don't.</p>
<p>I do agree with some of the criticism from Duhon though. I think the copies of the SCP need to be more consistent. Think about them thematically: Are they a representation of his subconscious? Are they actual other versions of himself?</p>
<p>Either way it's a bit much to go from all doom and gloom with messages that &quot;You should have done better&quot; to a message of hope all from the same source. I do think including a suicide attempt could be done well for this piece, but make sure it works out in as part of the emotional journey, positive or negative.</p>

