<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">[Placeholder from PM]</span></p>
<p>Hm. I like the premise here, although I'm not sure how popular it will be with the rest of the site. It's perhaps rather on the nose about what it's saying, but I kinda like what it's saying, and I think subtlety can be overrated sometimes.</p>
<p>The problems that he's encountered in his life here (alcoholism, bad job etc.) all feel very generic and impersonal to me. They don't feel specific to a character, at least as you've presented them here, and they feel too general to be making much of a thematic point.</p>
<p>The ending is also something I'm iffy on. Suicide is such a sensitive topic and I'm not sure the inclusion here is justified enough within the narrative. How do you plan to handle that sensitively and realistically?</p>
<p>It's also worth saying that this kind of article is going to be a particularly difficult one to pull off, especially as a new writer. Humanoids are widely considered the hardest to write because of all the work that needs to go into characterisation and believability, and this specific humanoid concept is particularly difficult in that regard. This isn't to put you off, necessarily, but a warning to be careful and to not expect this to be easy.</p>

							</div>

								
