			<div class="content" id="post-content-4733166">
									

<p>I've been watching this thread after our correspondence ended as the idea still interests me, and I think you've put work and thought into this idea; I think you have the skill necessary to produce a worthwhile draft. It's been fleshed out and focused in a good way, and I'm interested in seeing where this goes. Consider this a <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong>.</p>
<p>I would caution you to ensure that the emotion of the man comes through in a clear manner by telling the story largely from <em>his</em> perspective. The SCP format typically lends itself to stories told from the Foundation's perspective, which is some of the difficulty in writing emotional articles of this type in the format, but it's absolutely possible, and so long as you make good use of the storytelling devices available to you, I think you can convey it well.</p>

							</div>

								
					
